    "updated_at": "2026-11-09T23:56:52Z",
    "body": "Correction, self-caught while pinning: the issue body quotes the SetStock refusal as printing \"stock dimensions exceed 2000 mm\". It actually printed \"stock dimensions exceed 1e6 mm\" - MAX_STOCK_DIM is 1_000_000.0 and the old format used `{:e}`. PR #590 prints it through the lens instead: \"stock dimensions exceed 1000000 mm\" in mm mode. The tier-1 site list and the rest of the body stand; the quoted number was simply wrong.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
